recommendation:
Apply the Checks-Effects-Interactions pattern. Move `STORE.removeRentals` to execute BEFORE any external calls. Compute the order hash and rental asset updates first, then remove from storage, then execute hooks, reclaim, and settle. Additionally, add a reentrancy guard (nonReentrant modifier) to `stopRent` and `stopRentBatch`:


function stopRent(RentalOrder calldata order) external nonReentrant {
    _validateRentalCanBeStoped(...);
    // Build rentalAssetUpdates...
    // EFFECTS: Remove from storage FIRST
    STORE.removeRentals(_deriveRentalOrderHash(order), _convertToStatic(rentalAssetUpdates));
    // INTERACTIONS: Then external calls
    if (order.hooks.length > 0) { _removeHooks(...); }
    _reclaimRentedItems(order);
    ESCRW.settlePayment(order);
    _emitRentalOrderStopped(order.seaportOrderHash, msg.sender);
}

Add an explicit storage existence check at the beginning of `stopRent` and `stopRentBatch`, before any external interactions:


bytes32 orderHash = _deriveRentalOrderHash(order);
if (!STORE.isRentalOrder(orderHash)) {
    revert Errors.StopPolicy_OrderNotFound(orderHash);
}

This ensures all subsequent processing is for legitimate, active rental orders.
